ms in Mathematics and Mathematical Statistics at the University of Maryland offer rigorous training, a collaborative environment, and opportunities to advance your academic and professional career. Here are some reasons to consider joining us:\nRanked #1 in the country for the total number of minority students earning doctoral degrees in mathematics and statistics by Diverse: Issues in Higher Education.\nRanked #19 among the nation's top public institutions by U.S. News & World Report's 2021 Best Colleges.\nUseful Links\nLearn more about our graduate programs and the application process:\nGeneral Information Admission FAQ's\nHear from Our Students\n\"They prepared me not only for research but also for the job market. The logical thinking, problem-solving abilities, and communication skills I gained in grad school have been highly rewarding in my current position.\"\n\"Most students here are eager to help one another. My cohort is really open to collaboration\u2014no one is \u2018protective\u2019 of their knowledge. We succeed together.\"\nRead more about our student's experiences here.\nReady to Apply?\nIf you\u2019re passionate about mathematics and ready to take the next step in your academic and professional journey, we encourage you to apply. Our program will provide you with the tools and skills you need to succeed both in research and in your future career.\nStart Your Application Today\nMath Program\nStatistics Program\nAMSC\nMasters Along the Way\nCurrent Students\nProgress Toward Degree\nExams and Course Requirements\nCandidacy Requirements\nThesis and Dissertations\nCourse Information\nCurrent Classes\nUpcoming Classes\nArchived Courses\nProspective Students\nGeneral Information\nAdmissions\nFAQs\nStaff\nCareer Announcements (Internal)\nCareer & Professional Development\nGraduate Awards\nMathematics Graduate Program\nmathgrad@math.umd.edu\nStatistics Graduate Program\nstatgrad@math.umd.edu\nPH: 301.405.5058\nGraduate Office\nDepartment of Mathematics\n4176